A||||3||MinnGreenGT||Question of the "Unsure" headlight||||5||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||08-16-2001||11:46 AM||||I know headlight questions are common- and probably boring  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"> to most people, but this is a new one to me.<P>When I activate my headlights, they both begin to rise as normal. The Right Side (passenger's side) goes all the way up as usual. (Now the strange part) The Left side (driver's side) goes up about half way, then goes back down about an inch- back up 3/4 way, down an inch- then all the way up to it's locked position.<P>Are the bushings going bad (I don't hear anything unusual)? Something electrical? Help!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||5
Z||000001||Max The Chainsaw||08-16-2001||12:00 PM||||Sounds like the plastic bushings. I see by your sig that your car is an 87. That means newer style motors, which is a good thing. The newer style are a lot better motors as well as much easer and cheaper to repair. <P>Rodny Dickman (www.rodnydickman.com) sells a rebuild kit for these motors for about 5 bucks each, includes instructions. I'd recommend doing both motors.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||08-16-2001||12:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Max The Chainsaw:<BR><B>Sounds like the plastic bushings. I see by your sig that your car is an 87. That means newer style motors, which is a good thing. The newer style are a lot better motors as well as much easer and cheaper to repair. <P>Rodny Dickman (www.rodnydickman.com) sells a rebuild kit for these motors for about 5 bucks each, includes instructions. I'd recommend doing both motors.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yup, that sounds like it.  Those plastic bushing crack and turn to powder over time.  Just drop Rodney's replacements in and your back up and running.  $5 for one set, or do both headlights for $8.  What a bargain!  And it only takes about 10-20 minutes to do.||||reg||6
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-16-2001||01:14 PM||||also a lite coat of lithium grease on the slides on the bottom of the doors themselves.||||reg||1
